Stack: Node.js with pnpm. Create the manifest first with `pnpm init` (or a
framework starter such as `pnpm create vite`), then make sure `package.json`
defines the `dev`, `build`, `lint`, `typecheck` and `test` scripts that CI and the
commands below rely on. The manifest must also carry a `packageManager` field:
`pnpm init` on pnpm 9+ adds it automatically, otherwise add
`"packageManager": "pnpm@9"` by hand. `pnpm/action-setup@v4` in CI reads that field
to install the matching pnpm, and `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` needs a
committed lockfile — so run `pnpm install` and commit `package.json` and
`pnpm-lock.yaml` before expecting CI to pass.

```
pnpm install                  # install dependencies
pnpm dev                      # run locally
pnpm build                    # production build
pnpm test                     # full test suite
pnpm test -- <file-or-name>   # one test file or test name
pnpm lint                     # lint
pnpm typecheck                # type-check
```
